An ingest whose rotation fdatasync fails, with no memory to publish the
degraded state, throws std::bad_alloc in the I/O error's place. ingest_rotate
serves both the mid-slice rotation and the one after the last chunk.
Reverts #618.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: ingest whose rotation fdatasync fails"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
index 8b83e51..04b2981 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
@@ -222,8 +222,8 @@ void DB::ingest_rotate(TransientEngineState &t,
     t.active_file().sync();
     t.apply_sync(t.next_seq() - 1);
   } catch (...) {
-    degrade_from(current,
-                 "ingest rotation fdatasync failed: call resume() to recover.");
+    store_state(current->degraded_copy(
+        "ingest rotation fdatasync failed: call resume() to recover."));
     throw;
   }
   PreparedRotation rotation;
